  "worked_solution": "First, recall that\n\n$$\n{lim}_{s\\to 2}f(s)=\u27e8{lim}_{s\\to 2}{e}^{s-2},\\,{lim}_{s\\to 2}\\sqrt{6-s},\\,{lim}_{s\\to 2}\\frac{3}{s+2}\u27e9.\n$$\n\nNow, we find the limits one-by-one.\n\n- For the first component, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{s\\to 2}{e}^{s-2} & ={e}^{2-2} \\\\  & ={e}^{0} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For the second component, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{s\\to 2}\\sqrt{6-s} & =\\sqrt{6-2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For the third component, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{s\\to 2}\\frac{3}{s+2} & =\\frac{3}{2+2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, ${lim}_{s\\to 2}f(s)=\u27e81,2,\\frac{3}{4}\u27e9.$\n\nFinally, the limit of $\u2016f(s)\u2016$ as $s$ approaches $2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{s\\to 2}\u2016f(s)\u2016 & =\u2016{lim}_{s\\to 2}f(s)\u2016 \\\\  & =\u2016\u27e81,2,\\frac{3}{4}\u27e9\u2016 \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{(\\frac{3}{4})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+4+\\frac{9}{16}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{89}{16}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{89}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
